    "summary": "Man’s cloth, (Asante Kente), an &#039;asasia&#039; [see curatorial comment] cloth made of 23 narrow woven strips hand-woven from imported coloured industrial cotton thread, and hand-sewn together along the selvedges. The warp is of the ‘oyokoman’ pattern in red, yellow and green, and the length is divided into 52 small sections by thin lines of white thread. Each of the 52 sections in each strip has a variant pattern. The warp ends have been left as a fringe.",
